    "title": "A=1 core-one exceptional-trace nonvanishing",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On every official D_*=1 active core, the exceptional K trace is nonzero. A zero exceptional trace would force every domain trace active, Q(gamma_0;X) squarefree of degree r-1, and Q(gamma_0;X)A_a(gamma_0;X)=G_X. This requires X-degree D_0-r+1 in A_a, while X_0=1 and the original complement permit only D_0-r. Hence the zero-exceptional third system (ETA4) is empty, leaving only the D_*=0 and active-exceptional D_*=1 systems.",
